I’m testing a distinct gfx12-only state-load lever on `gated_delta_net_q8_fast`: replace four strided Q8 global byte loads per lane with one coalesced packed dword load, then transpose the four byte planes with wave shuffles. This preserves the signed-byte decode and all downstream arithmetic while reducing VMEM issue count; the non-gfx12 branch remains source-identical for absolute cross-arch isolation.
