codex
Hypothesis: at hot `K=2048`, Phase 1 already reads every `x` element, then Phase 2 reloads `x` and keeps eight prefetched `x` values live across the block reduction. I’ll reuse the Phase-1 values through gfx12-only LDS, using the existing reduction barrier for visibility. This is distinct from the dead unroll-8 lever: it trades one redundant L2 read plus long VGPR live ranges for LDS stores/reads without adding a barrier or changing arithmetic.
