codex
My lever is `res_rowphase_preload4`: keep the winning “memory phase then FMA phase” structure, but do it one output row at a time. That cuts simultaneously live weight headers from eight groups to four without changing any accumulator’s operation order. The expected mechanism is lower VGPR pressure and more TLP; if codegen remains at 72 VGPRs, the hypothesis predicts no lift.
