The harness verdict is `DEAD`: parity passed (`var_coh=OK`), but adaptive A/B found only +0.63% with f=0.569. Crucially, the compiler expanded the supposedly shorter live window from 72 to 96 VGPR, dropping occupancy to 20.9%; the kernel’s existing TLP already hides latency, so chunking did not expose a useful MLP lever. I’m recording that exact lesson in the required progress log.
