-// per-token requant (PARO path). This increased register pressure because
-// the compiler must carry the requant live-set (q0..q3, scale, rng, EF
-// temporaries) across the entire loop body. On gfx906 wave64 (256 VGPRs/file)
-// this causes spill-to-scratch: 108→172 bytes per workitem (+60%), costing
-// +38% per dispatch. This variant avoids that by keeping the loop lean.
-//
-// R13c3 lever (gfx1201): n_tokens==1 decode fast-path. BOD shows this
-// kernel at ~17% occ / ~33% mem_busy — grid under-subscription (heads×tiles)
-// makes per-block latency the limiter, not TLP. For decode, n_tokens is 1,
-// so the LDS S_tile round-trip (dequant→LDS→update→LDS→requant) is pure
-// overhead: chain dequant→update→requant in registers per row, identical
-// math, no LDS. Multi-token path retains the original LDS body.
 
