The counters show an L2-resident, partially memory-busy kernel (75.8% L2 hit, 43.5% memory busy) at 88 VGPRs, so I’m testing a narrow latency-hiding lever: pre-load only the next row’s packed 32-bit weight word while the current row’s eight dequantized MACs execute. This avoids previously dead row-count, launch-bound, metadata-broadcast, cache-bypass, X-prefetch, and reduction levers, while limiting added register pressure to roughly one packed word.
apply patch
