The distinct hypothesis is a gfx12-only `n_tokens == 1` direct-state path. Decode uses one token, yet the current kernel stages each Q8 state row into LDS, reloads it, writes the updated FP32 row back to LDS, then reloads it again for requantization. Processing and requantizing each row directly from registers removes that LDS round trip while preserving the exact dot/reduction/update/rounding order; the existing multi-token path remains unchanged, and the specialization will be preprocessor-gated to gfx12 so other architectures compile identically.
