I’m targeting `gated_delta_net_q8_fast` (the fewest adaptive dead attempts among the viable active choices). Its measured signature is L2-resident/mixed (`L2 85%`, `mem_busy 31.8%`, `VGPR 64`, `occ 16.5%`). The variant will make the four row-value loads lane-0-only and broadcast them within the wave, gated to gfx1200/1201 so other architectures compile identically. This is distinct from the dead gate/beta broadcast: it removes a redundant 16-byte per-lane vector fetch inside each token step.
