The RMS/rotate kernel is structurally under-occupied (one 256-thread block across 64 CUs), so added prefetch/MLP and LDS staging have already failed by raising VGPRs without creating more waves. I’m testing a new, register-neutral latency lever: on gfx12 only, apply the known ±1 FWHT signs by XORing the sign bit instead of issuing sixteen dependent floating multiplies per lane; other architectures retain byte-identical source behavior.
