I’m targeting `fused_rmsnorm_mq_rotate`. Its real limit is structural: one 256-thread block for decode, only ~0.1% device occupancy, with 18.1% memory busy. Prior dead attempts added live VGPRs or synchronization. My distinct hypothesis is an RDNA4-only cache-hint substitution: prefetch the first FWHT weight group with scalar `s_prefetch_data`, then load values after RMS publication, avoiding the long-lived weight/x register payload across both barriers while leaving all arithmetic and non-gfx12 code unchanged.
