I found a fresh, value-preserving lever: on gfx12 only, use DPP quad-permute for the XOR-1 and XOR-2 FWHT partner exchanges (`0xB1` and `0x4E`), while retaining `ds_swizzle` for XOR-4/8/16. This targets the one-block latency path, adds no persistent state, preserves the exact add/sub order, and leaves non-gfx12 compilation on the original bytecode path.
