   Make the learned= line specific — it is how the next round avoids re-deriving.

RIGOR: trust ONLY the harness verdict. PARITY_FAIL = your math changed the values; fix it to be exactly value-preserving; does NOT count as a lever tried. DEAD = value-preserving but no gain (or a loss); move on. INCONCLUSIVE = unresolved at the sampling cap; note it, do not re-try the same lever. A big delta with no mechanism to explain it = suspect a phantom; distrust it. Web search + web fetch are available — use them to check RDNA4 ISA / gfx1201 codegen specifics if it sharpens your hypothesis. Do EXACTLY ONE round then stop. End with a compact JSON: {"round_done":true,"kernel":<k>,"lever":<slug>,"verdict":<v>,"delta_pct":<d>,"learned":"<the bottleneck this round exposed>"}

