R21c1_rms_p1a_mid_pref kernel=fused_rmsnorm_mq_rotate lever=rms_p1a_mid_pref verdict=DEAD delta_pct=0.32 f=0.625 learned=Midpoint x/weight prefetch raised VGPR 48->56 and dropped occupancy 0.2->0.1%; this single-block RMS/FWHT kernel is structurally under-occupied, so extra live prefetch state overwhelms the latency-overlap benefit.
R27c0_res_curquad_spref kernel=gemv_hfq4g256_residual lever=res_curquad_spref verdict=DEAD delta_pct=0.69 f=0.609 learned=Gfx12 current-quad dual-row s_prefetch_data (g/g+2 × both rows during x-hoist; transfer of down g0_spref WIN) passed parity and held VGPR=72, but f=0.609 with profile_feedback=no clear lever signal (var wall 7.6% occ~6 mem_busy~9 L2~82 — no usable TLP/MLP shift). Residual is already L2-resident; first-demand weight-window hints do not expose a header-miss bottleneck, so both next-quad (R10c0) and current-quad s_prefetch are closed for this mixed GEMV.
