codex
I’m testing a narrow additive change on the current shared win: keep the gfx12 group-0 prefetch, but issue it only for rows 0–1. The hypothesis is that row 0–1 prefetches cover the first two independent 272-byte row streams, while their DOG work supplies enough latency for demand loads of rows 2–3; removing two scalar prefetch instructions may reduce front-end pressure without changing any output arithmetic. This is distinct from the historical prefetch experiments because it is layered on the certified four-row group-0 prefetch frontier.
