I’m testing one untried fused-kernel lever: for the hot `K=2048` shape, make each warp’s Phase-1 sum traverse the same 256-element group it owns in Phase 2, retaining those `x` vectors for FWHT. This removes the kernel’s full second read of `x` without adding a new prefetch ring or LDS state; other shapes retain the current path, and the source is already gfx12-specific. The reduction computes the same sum-of-squares, with only its parallel association changed, so exact token parity remains the deciding gate.
apply patch
