Hypothesis: Phase 1’s eight scalar loads per thread are latency-exposed because decode launches only one block. Rewriting only the gfx12 Phase-1 traversal as a pointer walk may remove repeated indexed-address formation without adding accumulators or changing reduction order; other architectures retain the original preprocessor branch byte-for-byte. This is deliberately narrower than the dead unroll, prefetch, vector-load, and reduction levers.
