codex
The chosen lever is a gfx12-only live-range compression: preserve the winning cross-barrier first-group prefetch, but immediately compute the original first multiply (`x * weight`) before the reduction. This retains identical left-associative math while carrying 8 products across the barriers instead of 16 separate x/weight values; the hypothesis is lower VGPR pressure without surrendering the latency overlap that the existing frontier won from.
